<h1>📺 How to Run the Phishinweather Broadcast</h1>
<p><em>Explain like I'm 10 edition</em></p>

<h2>What is this thing?</h2>

<p>Think of phishinweather.com like a TV station.</p>

<p>There's a <strong>director</strong> sitting in a control room — that's the server. The director decides what's on-air right now. Everyone watching, whether on YouTube or the website, sees the same screen at the same time. Just like a real TV channel.</p>

<p>You don't have to do anything for it to run. It just goes.</p>

<h2>Two channels</h2>

<div class="card">
  <div class="label">🎬 The Stream (YouTube)</div>
  <p>This is the broadcast. It runs a tight playlist: weather essentials, then a quick social bump (Instagram, YouTube, Reddit, Ko-fi), then Phish history and tour info, another bump, then countdown and live setlist. Social bumps are 5 seconds — just enough to remind people we exist, then back to content.</p>
  <p>Nobody can change it from the outside. It just plays.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="label">🖥️ The Website (phishinweather.com)</div>
  <p>When you open the site, you're tuned to the same screen as the stream — synchronized. But you have a remote. Press ◀ ▶ to look around. The <strong>◉ LIVE</strong> button (or pressing Play) snaps you back to what's on-air right now.</p>
  <p>Social cards play at full length (12 seconds) on the site since you chose to visit.</p>
</div>

<h2>Override controls</h2>

<p>Sometimes you want to interrupt the schedule. Go to <a href="/admin">/admin</a>, find the Broadcast Scheduler section, pick a screen, and hit one of these:</p>

<div class="card pin">
  <h3>📌 PIN — Freeze it here</h3>
  <p><strong>What it does:</strong> Holds that screen on both the stream and site until you click CLEAR. The normal schedule is paused.</p>
  <p><strong>Use it when:</strong> A show is about to start and you want to hold the "Phish Tour" card up. Or it's a big moment and you want everyone seeing the same thing indefinitely.</p>
  <p><strong>To release:</strong> Click <code>✕ CLEAR</code>. The schedule resumes where it left off.</p>
</div>

<div class="card push">
  <h3>⚡ PUSH — Show this right now</h3>
  <p><strong>What it does:</strong> Immediately cuts to that screen on both channels. Plays for one full duration, then the schedule automatically resumes. No CLEAR needed.</p>
  <p><strong>Use it when:</strong> A Ko-fi supporter just donated and you want to show the support card right now. Or you want to highlight something specific mid-broadcast.</p>
</div>

<div class="card queue">
  <h3>⏭ QUEUE — Play this next</h3>
  <p><strong>What it does:</strong> Waits for the current screen to finish naturally, then plays your queued screen once. Then back to normal.</p>
  <p><strong>Use it when:</strong> Something is almost done and you don't want to interrupt it. "Play the setlist card next." Clean, no jarring cuts.</p>
</div>

<h2>Step-by-step: how to use overrides</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Go to <a href="/admin">/admin</a></li>
  <li>Find the <strong>Broadcast Scheduler</strong> section at the top</li>
  <li>See what's currently on stream and site, and how many seconds are left</li>
  <li>Pick a screen from the dropdown</li>
  <li>Click PIN, PUSH, or QUEUE</li>
  <li>Click <strong>✕ CLEAR</strong> when you want to go back to the regular schedule</li>
</ol>

<h2>What's in each playlist?</h2>

<p><strong>Stream:</strong> Current Weather → Latest Obs → Local Forecast → Extended → Almanac → <em>Instagram bump (5s)</em> → Radar → Phish History → <em>YouTube bump (5s)</em> → Phish Tour → Countdown → Live Setlist → <em>Reddit bump (5s)</em> → <em>Ko-fi bump (5s)</em> → repeat</p>

<p><strong>Site:</strong> Current Weather → Latest Obs → Hourly → Hourly Graph → Local Forecast → Extended → Almanac → Phish History → Tour → Countdown → Live Setlist → Ko-fi → Instagram → YouTube → Reddit → Feature Vote → repeat</p>

<h2>What does "◉ LIVE" mean on the website?</h2>

<p>If you pressed ◀ or ▶ to browse around, you're no longer watching what the stream is showing. The red <strong>◉ LIVE</strong> button appears in the nav bar. Click it (or press Play) to snap back and re-sync with the broadcast.</p>

